<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexios III Angelos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1153–<a href="/years/1211">1211</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexios III Angelos was Byzantine emperor from 1195, after blinding and deposing his brother Isaac II. His weak rule allowed provincial lords such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-sgouros">Leo Sgouros</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dobromir-chrysos">Dobromir Chrysos</a> to set up their own lordships. He fled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a> arrived in 1203, and his son-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodore-i-laskaris">Theodore Laskaris</a> later founded the Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicaea">Nicaea</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexios-iii-angelos.jpg" alt="Alexios III Angelos" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown Byzantine scribes · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:145_-_Alexios_III_Angelos_(Mutinensis_-_color).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
